{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1394606-modifying-paradox-in-historical-settings-1910s-and-1940s","id":1394606,"title":"Modifying Paradox in historical settings (1910s and 1940s)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-06T12:35:43-07:00","id":1394606,"title":"Modifying Paradox in historical settings (1910s and 1940s)","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> Im running 2 parallel chronicles, one set in the 1910s and another in the 1940s. I started thinking today that the Paradox rules presented in M20 apply to the 21st century much in line with current scientific principles and dominant beliefs (arguably). I guess they shouldnt be applied to those times I mentioned strictly as they were written. I dont have enough general knowledge of the &quot;history of beliefs&quot; (to say it somehow) to say &quot;hey, people in the western world were believing these or those concepts in the 10s and 40s&quot;. As I know everything is about context, time and place, I would like to ask you:<br /> <br /> If you had to modify the Paradox rules (specially, how much Paradox one should earn for doing this or that) in those times - 1910s and 1940s - in the place you use as setting for your chronicle, how would you do it?<br /> <br /> PS - I havent read Sorcerers Crusade or Dark Ages Mage, so, no references for historical settings in Mage.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T12:59:21-07:00","id":1394610,"title":"","content":"Ok, I would take a look at actual fiction from those periods, and maybe some reference books for &quot;Call of Cthulhu&quot; (specially the Keeper's Companions and Atomic Age Cthulhu, which is set in the 50s).<br /> <br /> But, all in all, I don't think there should be a huge difference between the 40s and today... Maybe things would be more different in the 10s...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:58:01-07:00","id":1394662,"title":"","content":"There are some huge differences between the 1910s, 1940s and today.They are going to fall in transportation, electricity and computers.<br /> <br /> Transportationwise, cars are pretty primitive in the 1910s compared to today--you're just starting to see mass production. Gasoline is still pretty rare--not as rare as in the 1880s U.S. when the major petroleum product was kerosene for lighting but gasoline is going to be concentrated in certain areas where Standard Oil and other significant oil companies have built up retail routes. With Spindletop in Texas being drilled in 1901, the petroleum industry is still pretty much in its infancy in much of the U.S. Electricity is not common in the U.S. in 1910 and you've got coal-fired plants as your basic plant except in places with abundant hydropower resources like Wisconsin (lots of small waterfalls) and no nuclear plants or solar plants. Most people don't own many electrical devices--you aren't even to half of homes in the U.S. having electricity until the 1940s when New Deal money for homes (FHA among others) and big dam projects promotes electrification. In both periods, there's not any computer network as we know it and any computing machines are more likely to be people with math skills.<br /> <br /> Paradox should always reflect what is the local reality zone. I'd make Forces effects involving electric and effects involving cars more difficult. As for histories, consider just looking up a general history survey or something on urban history for the area you are setting the game in.<br /> <br /> For a few works on the growth of energy in western society, links below. If you have a friend with a college account, Networks of Power is part of the American Council of Learned Society e-book program. . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Networks-Power-Electrification-1880-1930-Softshell/dp/0801846145/ref=pd_lpo_14_t_1/146-3353322-5766405?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=0801846145&amp;pd_rd_r=ce57a01d-7d91-47c6-8e15-1a201d6e413d&amp;pd_rd_w=pMh55&amp;pd_rd_wg=H2YGj&amp;pf_rd_p=7b36d496-f366-4631-94d3-61b87b52511b&amp;pf_rd_r=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Networks-Power-Electrification-1880-1930-Softshell/dp/0801846145/ref=pd_lpo_14_t_1/146-3353322-5766405?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=0801846145&amp;pd_rd_r=ce57a01d-7d91-47c6-8e15-1a201d6e413d&amp;pd_rd_w=pMh55&amp;pd_rd_wg=H2YGj&amp;pf_rd_p=7b36d496-f366-4631-94d3-61b87b52511b&amp;pf_rd_r=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Networks-Power-Electrification-1880-1930-Softshell/dp/0801846145/ref=pd_lpo_14_t_1/146-3353322-5766405?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=0801846145&amp;pd_rd_r=ce57a01d-7d91-47c6-8e15-1a201d6e413d&amp;pd_rd_w=pMh55&amp;pd_rd_wg=H2YGj&amp;pf_rd_p=7b36d496-f366-4631-94d3-61b87b52511b&amp;pf_rd_r=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Networks-Power-Electrification-1880-1930-Softshell/dp/0801846145/ref=pd_lpo_14_t_1/146-3353322-5766405?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=0801846145&amp;pd_rd_r=ce57a01d-7d91-47c6-8e15-1a201d6e413d&amp;pd_rd_w=pMh55&amp;pd_rd_wg=H2YGj&amp;pf_rd_p=7b36d496-f366-4631-94d3-61b87b52511b&amp;pf_rd_r=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=ZAGXZ7WSHK5WS83HTNJP </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Electrifying-America-Meanings-Technology-1880-1940/dp/0262640309\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Electrifying-America-Meanings-Technology-1880-1940/dp/0262640309\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Electrifying-America-Meanings-Technology-1880-1940/dp/0262640309\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Electrifying-America-Meanings-Technology-1880-1940/dp/0262640309 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T22:19:19-07:00","id":1394722,"title":"","content":"For those sorts of things I tend to follow these rules of thumb:<br /> <br /> For technology, or technomagic, what could be the next logical step in current familiar technology in use or well known scientific knowledge is coincidental. Anything further is vulgar. <br /> <br /> For mystic weirdness, it's coincidental if most of the people in the local region thinks that sort of thing could happen, regardless of the era. <br /> <br /> So for 1910 this would likely mean that in &quot;civilized areas&quot; early airplanes, powered lighter than air vehicles, and electric appliances that act like older tools are mostly coincidental, but things like jet planes and plastic, and Jules Verne style supersonic vehicles or submarines are vulgar.<br /> <br /> By 1940, world war 1 had ended and crazy heavy planes, submarines, and things only invented before or early in WW2 would probably be coincidental. Supersonic flight would still be vulgar for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T12:02:52-07:00","id":1394837,"title":"","content":"Trade organization periodicals and magazines such as Popular Science might be a good way to see what is 'out there' technology and what is 'around the corner.'<br /> <br /> For example, although we think smart meters for electricity and natural gas demand are a modern thing using computers, mechanical regulation of natural gas demand was something feasible in the 1910s. So were electric cars--the electric power companies were promoting them in their trade magazines.<br /> <br /> Here's a google books excerpt from Electric Vehicles, which was a trade association. One of the major energy magnates in the U.S., Henry Latham Doherty, though appearing sporadically in the publication, heavily promoted electric vehicles where his companies offered electric service.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=tylMAQAAMAAJ&amp;pg=PA194&amp;lpg=PA194&amp;dq=henry+l+doherty+electric+vehicles&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=yGIHCtmdWJ&amp;sig=ACfU3U0wtP4kgX9sGDq-syC1Pi1K9GBRHQ&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjF6JOtrPDpAhW6FTQIHcPvCBwQ6AEwDHoECAcQAQ#v=onepage&amp;q=henry%20l%20doherty%20electric%20vehicles&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://books.google.com/books/content?id=tylMAQAAMAAJ&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;img=1&amp;zoom=1&amp;edge=curl&amp;imgtk=AFLRE70oMxb58d5l5BL6gOMF7DLLAI1orXgYy3l-6N3vMMvUMC8JzIDDKrzZLlGp68ze4gD6h_NEgqOpS3fT1GUKBkh64w8G8szGIkS12xQp7US1h67Ar_zYIagZ4SEMkqGIBhpCCBeV\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=tylMAQAAMAAJ&amp;pg=PA194&amp;lpg=PA194&amp;dq=henry+l+doherty+electric+vehicles&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=yGIHCtmdWJ&amp;sig=ACfU3U0wtP4kgX9sGDq-syC1Pi1K9GBRHQ&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjF6JOtrPDpAhW6FTQIHcPvCBwQ6AEwDHoECAcQAQ#v=onepage&amp;q=henry%20l%20doherty%20electric%20vehicles&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\"> Ignition and Accessories </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=tylMAQAAMAAJ&amp;pg=PA194&amp;lpg=PA194&amp;dq=henry+l+doherty+electric+vehicles&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=yGIHCtmdWJ&amp;sig=ACfU3U0wtP4kgX9sGDq-syC1Pi1K9GBRHQ&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjF6JOtrPDpAhW6FTQIHcPvCBwQ6AEwDHoECAcQAQ#v=onepage&amp;q=henry%20l%20doherty%20electric%20vehicles&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\"> https://books.google.com/books?id=tylMAQAAMAAJ&amp;pg=PA194&amp;lpg=PA194&amp;dq=henry+l+doherty+electric+vehicles&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=yGIHCtmdWJ&amp;sig=ACfU3U0wtP4kgX9sGDq-syC1Pi1K9GBRHQ&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjF6JOtrPDpAhW6FTQIHcPvCBwQ6AEwDHoECAcQAQ#v=onepage&amp;q=henry%20l%20doherty%20electric%20vehicles&amp;f=false </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Before World War I, there's more hope in the United States. It's the 'Progressive Era' and science and technology were seen as more likely to solve humanity's problems. Once World War I starts, although science and technology were still progressing, much of the hope was lost--the 1920s are an interesting decade where corporate interests (all very capitalist laissez-faire Republican administrations in the 1920s) and fundamentalism (Scopes trial amongst others) and racism (big decade for the Klu Klux Klan) push back reform.<br /> <br /> For other countries, read up on what's going on in their major publications or newspapers. For the electric utility industry, another source you can use is Alfred Chandler's <i>Scale and Scope: The Dynamics of Industrial Capitalism</i>. Chandler compares several industries in the U.S., Great Britain and Germany.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Scale-Scope-Dynamics-Industrial-Capitalism/dp/0674789954\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Scale-Scope-Dynamics-Industrial-Capitalism/dp/0674789954\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Scale-Scope-Dynamics-Industrial-Capitalism/dp/0674789954\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Scale-Scope-Dynamics-Industrial-Capitalism/dp/0674789954 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:48:27-07:00","id":1395407,"title":"","content":"I would suggest using the divisions of Subtle/Uncanny/Extreme, as presented in &quot;Mage Made Easy&quot;. I introduced the concept to my group yesterday, and they gave it the stamp of approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}